5).\n   - Erin is round (fact 6).\n\n2. **Applying the rules**:\n   - Since Erin is rough (fact 5), **Rule 8** (\"All rough people are green\") confirms she is green, consistent with fact 4.\n   - **Rule 9** states \"If someone is green, then they are white.\" Since Erin is green, she must be **white**.\n   - **Rule 10** (\"If someone is white, then they are not big\") means Erin is **not big**.\n   - **Rule 11** (\"If someone is green and not big, then they are kind\") applies here because Erin is green and not big. Thus, Erin must be **kind**.\n   - **Rule 12** (\"If someone is kind and not big, then they are round\") also applies, confirming Erin is round (fact 6 is consistent).\n\n3. **Key conclusion**:\n   - Erin must be white due to Rule 9. The statement \"Erin is not white\" directly contradicts this conclusion. Therefore, the statement is **false**.\n\n4. **Addressing potential confusion**:\n   - Erin\u2019s inferred \"kind\" status (via Rule 11) isn\u2019t explicitly stated in the context, but rules override explicit gaps to maintain consistency. The problem requires using all given rules and facts together, so Erin being kind is logically necessary and valid.\n\n**Answer**: B) False.",
