      "text": " The statement \"Erin is not young\" is false, so the correct answer is B) False.\n\nWait, but maybe I missed something. Let me think again. Let me go through step by step again in bullet points:\n\n- Erin's given: cold, rough.\n- From 7 (All cold are white), so Erin is white.\n- From 6 (if cold and white \u2192 quiet), so Erin is quiet.\n- From 9 (white and quiet \u2192 smart), so Erin is smart.\n- From 5 (smart and rough \u2192 young), so Erin is young.\n- Therefore, \"Erin is not young\" is false. So answer B.\n\nYes, that seems solid. So the correct answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe context provides the following relevant information about Erin:\n- Erin is **cold** and **rough** (given directly).\n- Since all cold people are **white** (point 7), Erin is **white**.\n- Erin being cold and white triggers point 6: cold + white \u2192 **quiet**. Thus, Erin is **quiet**.\n- Erin being white and quiet triggers point 9: white + quiet \u2192 **smart**. Thus, Erin is **smart**.\n- Now, Erin is **smart** and **rough**, so point 5 applies: all smart, rough people are **young**. Therefore, Erin must be **young**.\n\nThe statement \"Erin is not young\" directly contradicts this conclusion. Hence, the statement is **false**.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
