e 15 (\"If someone is kind, then they like the lion\") requires the kind mouse to like the lion.\n\n4. **Lion\u2019s Color**:\n   - Premise 14 (\"If someone likes the lion, then the lion is green\") now applies because the mouse (someone) likes the lion. Thus, the lion must be green.\n\n**Conclusion**: The lion is green, so the statement \"The lion is not green\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: B) False",
