ed.\"  \n   Anne is rough and nice, so she must be **red**.\n\n3. **Rule 4:** \"Red people are smart.\"  \n   Since Anne is red, she must be **smart**.\n\n4. **Rule 8:** \"All smart people are quiet.\"  \n   Since Anne is smart, she must be **quiet**.\n\n5. **Rule 5:** \"If someone is smart and quiet, they are cold.\"  \n   Anne is both smart and quiet, so she must also be **cold**.\n\n### **Checking for Contradictions:**\n- **Rule 1:** \"Cold people are young.\"  \n  Anne is cold and young, so no conflict here.\n- **Rule 7:** \"All red, quiet people are cold.\"  \n  Anne is red, quiet, and cold, so this holds.\n- **Rule 3:** \"Cold, red people are smart.\"  \n  Anne is cold, red, and smart, which aligns with this rule.\n\n### **Conclusion:**\nAll rules consistently lead to Anne being **smart**. Therefore, the statement \"Anne is not smart\" is **false**.\n\n### **Answer:**  \n**B) False**",
