is quiet. This attribute is explicitly given and is part of the premises.\n- While the contradiction about Gary\u2019s color (white vs. red) exists, it does not affect the validity of his quietness. The contradiction arises from conflicting rules about his color, not his quietness.\n- Since the question asks specifically about quietness, the direct statement that Gary is quiet must hold true unless explicitly negated by a rule. No rule negates Gary\u2019s quietness.\n\n### **Conclusion:**\nThe contradiction in Gary\u2019s color does not invalidate his explicitly stated quietness. Therefore, the statement \"Gary is not quiet\" is **false** because the context confirms he is quiet. \n\n**Answer:** B) False",
