omeone is quiet and round, they are red (Rule 6)*, Dave must be **red**.  \n   - Since Dave is **red and round**, the rule *If someone is red and round, they are smart (Rule 2)* makes him **smart**.  \n\n2. **Deductions for Niceness**:  \n   - Dave is now **quiet**, **smart**, **red**, **round**, and **green**.  \n   - The rule *All quiet, smart people are nice (Rule 9)* applies here. Since Dave is both **quiet** and **smart**, he must be **nice**.  \n\n3. **Conclusion**:  \n   - The statement \"Dave is not nice\" is **false** because the rules force Dave to be nice based on his attributes.  \n\n**Answer**: B) False.",
