 rough, then Harry is red\" (statement 12), Harry is red.\n   - Since Harry is red, \"Red people are blue\" (statement 10) makes him blue.\n   - Harry is now both blue and red, so \"Blue, red people are white\" (statement 14) means he is white.\n   - Harry is now white and rough. The rule \"White, rough people are kind\" (statement 13) requires him to be kind.\n\n2. **Conclusion:**\n   - Harry must be kind. Therefore, the statement \"Harry is not kind\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
