le \"If something is rough and green, then it is round\" (statement 5) would require her to be round. \n4. **Consistency Check for Roundness**: There is no explicit contradiction here. To avoid violating statement 5, Fiona must be round. This is permissible because no rule prohibits her from being round. Moreover, being round would also satisfy \"Round things are green\" (statement 10), aligning with her greenness from quietness. Thus, there is no contradiction.\n5. **No Conflicting Rules**: Fiona\u2019s other attributes (not nice, rough) do not override her greenness. For example, \"All nice things are blue\" (statement 11) does not apply, and her roughness does not conflict with greenness unless combined with rules requiring blue or other colors, which are not triggered here.\n\nSince Fiona must be green due to being quiet, the statement \"Fiona is not green\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
