ing is cold and chases the cat, it sees the cat\"), the tiger must see the cat.\n\n3. **Verification**:\n   - If the tiger sees the cat, conditional 17 (\"If something sees the cat, the cat is big\") requires the cat to be big. While the cat\u2019s size isn\u2019t explicitly stated, the conditional enforces this conclusion without contradiction (the cat\u2019s youth and roughness remain unaffected).\n\n**Conclusion**: The tiger sees the cat, so the statement \"The tiger does not see the cat\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: B) False.",
