 (who needs the bald eagle and now sees the lion by Premise 12) must see the cow. Thus, the lion sees the cow.  \n\n4. **Applying Premise 11**:  \n   Because the lion (someone) sees the cow, Premise 11 triggers the conclusion that the cow needs the bald eagle.  \n\nThis chain of reasoning confirms that **the cow needs the bald eagle**. Therefore, the statement \"The cow does not need the bald eagle\" is **false**.  \n\n**Answer**: B) False",
