s quiet and not smart, then it is kind.\"*\n   - Gary is **quiet** (from step 2) and **not kind** (he is \"nice,\" not \"kind\").\n   - To avoid contradicting Rule 11, Gary must be **smart** (so the antecedent of Rule 11, \"not smart,\" does not hold).\n\n4. **Consistency with Other Rules**:\n   - Rule 12 (\"Smart things are quiet\") is satisfied since Gary is both **smart** and **quiet**.\n   - Rule 10 (\"Rough, quiet things are not kind\") holds because Gary is **rough** and **quiet** but not **kind**.\n   - No other rules conflict with this conclusion.\n\n**Conclusion**: Gary is **quiet**. Therefore, the statement *\"Gary is not quiet\"* is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: B) False.",
