t\'s see if there\'s any rule that would make him not blue. Suppose Dave is blue. Let\'s see:.\n\nIs there any rule that would require him to be something that contradicts his known attributes?.\n\nAlternatively, maybe if he were blue, then some other condition would be triggered. Let\'s see.\n\nLooking at the rules again:.\n\nRule 10: If Dave is blue, then he must be furry. Which he is, so that\'s okay.\n\nRule 15: Blue and round → not quiet. But Dave\'s roundness is unknown. So unless we can find that Dave is round, then even if he were blue, that rule wouldn\'t apply. Since he\'s not stated to be round, that\'s okay.\n\nWait, but is there any rule that would require Dave to be round or not?.\n\nLooking at the context, Dave\'s properties are only big, furry, cold, rough. Roundness isn\'t mentioned. So Dave could be round or not, unless inferred.\n\nWait, rule 9: Quiet and big → not round. Dave is not quiet, so that doesn\'t apply. So Dave\'s roundness is unknown.\n\nHmm. So assuming Dave is blue doesn\'t lead to any contradictions based on the given rules. Therefore, is there any rule that would prevent Dave from being blue?.\n\nAlternatively, maybe we can find that Dave must not be blue. Let\'s see.\n\nWait, rule 14 says all big things are cold. Dave is big and cold. Rule 16 says cold things are rough. So Dave is rough. Now, if something is rough and cold (which Dave is), then by rule 8, it must be furry, which he is. So that\'s okay.\n\nNow, let\'s consider another angle. Let\'s see if there are any other rules that involve blue and other attributes.\n\nRule 3 says Erin is blue. So Erin is blue, and she\'s also cold and round. From rule 15, blue and round things are not quiet. Since Erin is blue and round, she can\'t be quiet, which is consistent because she isn\'t listed as quiet. So that\'s okay.\n\nAnother thing: Rule 13 says that quiet things are cold. Fiona is quiet (from 6), so Fiona must be cold. Fiona\'s coldness isn\'t stated, but according to rule 13, she must be cold. So Fiona is cold.\n\nAlso, Fiona is quiet. Rule 11 says quiet and blue things must be big. So if Fiona is blue, then she must be big. But Fiona\'s bigness isn\'t stated. So unless Fiona is blue, her bigness is unknown. But Fiona\'s furrieness is also a factor here. Rule 12: If Fiona is furry, then she is blue. So if Fiona were furry, she would have to be blue, but if she\'s not furry, that doesn\'t say anything.\n\nBut Fiona\'s properties are only that she\'s quiet. So she must be cold (from rule 13). So Fiona is quiet, cold, and maybe other attributes.\n\nBack to Dave. Let\'s see if there\'s any other constraints. Suppose Dave is blue. Then, since he\'s big (given), blue, and big. Let\'s see if there\'s a rule that links blue and big with something else. For instance, rule 11: quiet and blue → big. Since he\'s not quiet, that\'s okay. .\n\nAlternatively, if something is blue and big, does any rule apply? Not directly. The only rules involving blue and another attribute are:.\n\n- Blue and quiet → big (rule 11).\n- Blue and round → not quiet (rule15).\n- Fiona\'s case: if furry → blue (rule12).\n\nSo Dave being blue and big doesn\'t conflict with any rules. .\n\nWait another thought: All big things are cold (rule14). Since Dave is big and cold, and cold implies rough (rule16), so he\'s rough. Now, if he were blue, then perhaps there\'s another path. Let me see.\n\nWait, is there a rule that says blue things can\'t be big? No, the rules don\'t say that. So being blue and big is allowed unless there\'s a contradiction.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the contrapositive of some other rule? Let me check.\n\nRule 15: Blue and round → not quiet. But Dave isn\'t necessarily round. So even if he were blue, unless he\'s round, that\'s okay.\n\nHmm. So I can\'t find any rule that would make Dave being blue impossible. Therefore, Dave could be blue, and there\'s no contradiction. But then why is the question asking whether "Dave is not blue" is true, false, or unknown?.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there\'s a way to prove that Dave cannot be blue, making the statement "Dave is not blue" true.\n\nWait, let me think again. Let me see if there\'s a way that Dave must not be blue.\n\nSuppose Dave is blue. Then, since he is big, blue, and big. Let\'s see if any other rules come into play. For example, rule 11: Quiet and blue → big. But since Dave isn\'t quiet, that\'s okay.\n\nWait, but maybe Fiona\'s situation? Not sure.\n\nAlternatively, if Dave is blue and big, then since he\'s big, he\'s cold (rule14), so he\'s cold. But if something is cold, it\'s rough (rule16). So he\'s rough. All that\'s consistent with what\'s given.\n\nAlternatively, is there a rule that says something else? Let me check all again.\n\nRule 9: Quiet and big → not round. Dave isn\'t quiet, so that\'s okay.\n\nRule 10: If Dave is blue → furry. Since he\'s already furry, that holds.\n\nHmm. So there\'s no contradiction in assuming Dave is blue. So then, is there any rule that would require Dave to not be blue?.\n\nAlternatively, maybe through another path. Let\'s see:.\n\nSuppose Dave is blue. Then, since he\'s blue and big, is there any rule that would require him to be something else?.\n\nWait, rule 15: blue and round → not quiet. But unless he\'s round, that doesn\'t apply. Since his roundness isn\'t known, that\'s okay.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Fiona\'s attributes? Not sure.\n\nWait, another angle: Fiona is quiet, so she must be cold (rule13). Since Fiona is quiet, rule11 says if she\'s blue, then she must be big. But Fiona\'s bigness is not stated. So if Fiona is blue, then she must be big. But we don\'t know if Fiona is blue. Fiona\'s furrieness determines that via rule12: if Fiona is furry, then she\'s blue. But Fiona\'s furrieness isn\'t stated. So Fiona could be either furry or not. If she\'s not furry, then rule12 doesn\'t force her to be blue. So Fiona\'s blueness is unknown unless we have more info.\n\nBut this seems unrelated to Dave\'s blueness.\n\nWai