nally, the rules do not create any contradictions that would invalidate this fact. \n\n### Key Analysis:\n1. **Harry\u2019s Attributes**: \n   - Harry is explicitly stated to be **cold** (point 6) and **white** (point 7).\n   - By rule 15 (\"All cold, white people are rough\"), Harry must also be **rough** (since he is cold and white).\n   - By rule 8 (\"All rough people are furry\"), Harry must also be **furry** (since he is rough).\n\n2. **Consistency with Rules**:\n   - Rule 9 (\"If someone is rough and cold, they are white\") is satisfied because Harry is rough, cold, and white.\n   - No rule contradicts Harry\u2019s stated attributes (cold, white) or inferred attributes (rough, furry).\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The statement \"Harry is not white\" directly contradicts the explicit information that Harry is white. Thus, it is **false**.\n\n### Answer:\n**B) False**",
