messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is nice. Bob is round. Bob is young. Dave is round. Erin is big. Erin is red. Gary is young. All round things are nice. All nice, big things are white. If something is big and white then it is round. Young things are nice. Big, red things are young. All nice things are quiet. All quiet things are big. Young, quiet things are red.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: C\n', '<think>:.\nOkay, let\'s try to tackle this problem step by step. First, I need to understand all the given information and then see how it applies to Gary\'s size. The question is whether Gary is big, and the options are True, False, or Unknown. Let\'s start by listing all the facts provided.\n\nFirst, the context gives us several statements about different individuals (Bob, Dave, Erin, Gary) and categories (round, nice, young, big, red, white, quiet). Let me parse each one carefully.\n\n1. Bob is nice.\n2. Bob is round.\n3. Bob is young.\n4. Dave is round.\n5. Erin is big.\n6. Erin is red.\n7. Gary is young.\n8. All round things are nice.\n9. All nice, big things are white.\n10. If something is big and white then it is round.\n11. Young things are nice.\n12. Big, red things are young.\n13. All nice things are quiet.\n14. All quiet things are big.\n15. Young, quiet things are red.\n\nThe question is about Gary being big. Let\'s see what we know about Gary. From statement 7, Gary is young. Now, let\'s see if we can link this to being big.\n\nLooking at statement 11: Young things are nice. Since Gary is young, he must be nice (from 11). So Gary is nice and young. .\n\nNow, statement 13 says all nice things are quiet. Since Gary is nice, he must also be quiet. So Gary is quiet. .\n\nNow, statement 