ait, but let me check again for any possible contradictions that would make the statement false. Suppose the rules somehow made it impossible for Gary to be furry given his other attributes? Let\'s see: Gary is green, young, and furry. From rule 5, he must be blue. From rule 13, since he\'s blue and young, he must be red. So he must be red as well. But the context doesn\'t say he\'s red, but that\'s okay because the context only lists some of his attributes. The question is only about being furry, which is stated. So no contradiction there. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
