on chases the squirrel → squirrel must visit the cat (point 20). .\n\n- Squirrel visits cat → must like cat (point 14). .\n\n- Squirrel likes cat → must chase itself (point 17). .\n\nYes, this seems correct. .\n\nTherefore, the squirrel must chase itself, making the original statement false. .\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) False. .\n\nBut wait, let\'s check if there\'s any contradictions here. .\n\nThe squirrel is forced to chase itself because of the chain, but does that cause any issues?.\n\nIf the squirrel chases itself, then point 20 says it must visit the cat, which we already have. .\n\nAnd visiting the cat requires liking the cat, which is already in place. .\n\nSo it\'s a consistent loop. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 57%|#####6    | 342/600 [4:58:09<4:06:14, 57.27s/it]
