*young (Y)** and **cold (C)**.  \n   - From the rule **\"If something is young, then it is smart\"** (Y \u2192 S), Gary must be **smart (S)** because he is young.\n\n2. **Applying Rule 7**:  \n   - The rule **\"All smart, young things are nice\"** (S \u2227 Y \u2192 N) applies to Gary. Since he is both **smart (S)** and **young (Y)**, he must be **nice (N)**.  \n\n3. **Additional Checks**:  \n   - **Rule 8** states that if something is **nice and smart**, it must be **round (R)**. Since Gary is inferred to be nice and smart, he must also be round. However, this does not conflict with any given information.  \n   - **Rule 3** (Gk \u2227 Gc \u2192 Gr) requires Gary to be rough if he is both kind and cold. Since his kindness is not established, this rule does not affect the conclusion about his niceness.  \n\nNo contradictions arise from these deductions. The premises logically necessitate that Gary is nice.  \n\n**Answer**: A) True.",
