should be B.\n</think>\n\nThe context explicitly states, \"The dog is blue,\" making the statement \"The dog is not blue\" **false**. While the conditional rules introduce implications (e.g., the dog must eat the cat because it is blue), these do not contradict the direct statement about the dog's color. All inferred facts align with the dog being blue without creating inconsistencies. \n\n**Answer:** B) False.",
