hings are furry. Since Dave is cold, he must be **furry**.  \n\n3. **Additional Checks**:  \n   - **Rule 3**: Furry, round things are big. This rule is redundant here because Dave\u2019s bigness is already established by Rule 2.  \n   - **Rule 6**: Furry, big things are young. While this means Dave must also be young (inferred but not explicitly stated), it doesn\u2019t negate the conclusion that he is furry.  \n\nNo contradictions arise from the rules, and all deductions logically follow. Thus, **Dave must be furry**.\n\n**Answer**:  \nA) True",
