her connection.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the contrapositive of some rule can be applied. Let me think of the rules again.\n\nThe rule "If Fiona is rough and cold then Fiona is smart." Since Fiona is smart, could that mean she must be rough and cold? No, because that\'s the converse. The rule is if A then B, but B being true doesn\'t require A. So Fiona being smart doesn\'t require her to be rough and cold. So that doesn\'t help.\n\nAlternatively, the rule "Cold, furry things are white" is applied to Fiona, which is correct.\n\nHmm. I think the conclusion is that Fiona\'s age isn\'t determined by the given information. Therefore, the statement "Fiona is not young" is unknown. So the answer is C) Unknown.\n\nWait, but wait a second. Let me check another angle. The question is whether Fiona is NOT young. So if we can prove that Fiona is young, then the statement would be false. If we can prove she is not young, then it\'s true. If neither, then unknown.\n\nWait, perhaps there\'s a way to show that Fiona must be young? Let me see.\n\nSuppose Fiona is not young. Then she isn\'t young. But is there any rule that could conflict with her attributes?.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Fiona\'s being smart and cold allows her to be young or not. Let me think of Erin, who is young and smart. Fiona is also smart and cold. But Erin has additional traits like nice and rough. Fiona doesn\'t. So unless there\'s a rule that says all smart, cold things must be young, which there isn\'t. The only rules about youth are the ones mentioned before.\n\nHmm. I think I have to go with C) Unknown. But let me double-check.\n\nWait, another thought: The rule "All rough, nice things are young." So if Fiona were rough and nice, she would have to be young, but she isn\'t. So that doesn\'t affect her.\n\nAnother possible path: Since Fiona is smart and cold, and smart things are cold, but that doesn\'t relate to age.\n\nWait, maybe the contrapositive of "Young things are cold" is "If not cold, then not young." Since Fiona is cold, that doesn\'t give info. So Fiona could be young or not. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
