it must be cold. It doesn\'t say that being cold makes it kind. Wait, actually, the first rule is "Kind things are cold." So that\'s a one-way implication: if something is kind, then it is cold. But being cold doesn\'t necessarily make it kind. The other rules like "Red, furry things are kind" give other ways to be kind. But in Gary\'s case, he\'s kind, so that requires him to be cold. So there\'s no way around it. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
