 - From **Premise 7** (lion sees the bald eagle) and **Premise 10**, the lion must **need itself** (since seeing the bald eagle implies needing the lion).\n   - The lion now **needs both the bear (Premise 6) and itself**. Applying **Premise 11**, this means **the bear is round**.\n   - Since the bear is round (**from Premise 11**), **Premise 8** requires the bear to **see the bald eagle**.\n   - From the bear seeing the bald eagle (**via Premise 8**) and **Premise 10**, the bear must **need the lion**.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The bear **does need the lion**, so the statement \"The bear does not need the lion\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: B) False.",
