e Bob to be white if he is green and round, this does not conflict with his being green. The question only asks about his color (green), not other attributes like whiteness or size.\n- **Rule 16** (smart and white things are big) and **Rule 20** (big things are nice) apply to Bob if he is white and smart, but these do not negate his greenness.\n\nNo contradictions arise from these deductions. Therefore, **Bob must be green** based on the provided rules.\n\n**Answer**: A) True",
